    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his score of 81.45 is driven by elite xwOBA metrics and a favorable matchup against Houser, making him our primary offensive engine. **Junior Caminero** follows as a high-value play at 67.62, benefiting significantly from park factors and a prime #3 hole projection against Perkins. We are also leaning heavily into **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.45), both of whom benefit from weak SP_xERA figures\u2014Feltner and Leahy respectively\u2014that allow them to capitalize on high-ceiling environments. While **Trea Turner** carries a lower score of 59.89 due to the difficulty of stealing bases against a high-hold pitcher, his #2 spot in the order remains vital to our overall run production.\n\nStrategic roster construction for today hinges on our approach to scarcity. We have prioritized **Dillon Dingler** (58.63) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.33) despite the inherent volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as their speed profiles against specific delivery tendencies remain crucial to maintaining our SB floor. **Gary Sanchez** provides a surprising boost at 61.72, as his raw power profile matches up efficiently against Ray. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Smith**, who sits at 34.80; while he offers late-inning flexibility, the optimizer penalized his expected #8 batting position and a stiff matchup against the southpaw Suarez, forcing us to favor the higher-upside platoon splits offered by **Lars Nootbaar** and **Carson Benge**. Note that **Casey Schmitt** remains unavailable due to his IL designation, while **Christian Yelich** and **Nelson Velazquez** are confirmed out of the starting rotation today, necessitating a conservative approach to our game caps.",
